  "answer_text": "Because I am an AI assistant, I cannot directly buy the tickets or process payments on your behalf. However, I can help you find the right schedule and guide you on exactly how to book your trip. \n\nSince today is Sunday, June 7, 2026, \"next Friday\" could refer to either **Friday, June 12, 2026** (this upcoming Friday) or **Friday, June 19, 2026**. \n\n### 1. Choose Your Train Service\nAmtrak offers two main train options between Boston (South Station - BOS) and New York (Moynihan Train Hall at Penn Station - NYP):\n* **Northeast Regional:** Takes about **4 hours and 15 minutes**. It is the most common and budget-friendly choice (typically starting around $27\u2013$50 one-way if booked in advance, though Friday peak tickets may cost more).\n* **Acela (High-Speed):** Takes about **3 hours and 30 minutes**. It is a premium, business-focused train with fewer stops, though tickets are significantly more expensive.\n\n### 2. Choose Your Friday Dates\nDepending on when you plan to travel and return:\n* **Option A (This coming Friday):** Depart Friday, June 12, 2026 | Return Friday, June 12, 2026 (or later in the weekend).\n* **Option B (The following Friday):** Depart Friday, June 19, 2026 | Return Friday, June 19, 2026 (or later in the weekend).\n\n### 3. How to Book Your Return Ticket\nYou can book your round-trip ticket directly in just a few minutes:\n\n1. **Go to the Official Site:** Visit the [Amtrak Website](https://www.amtrak.com) or download the Amtrak mobile app.\n2. **Select Round-Trip:** Toggle the search tool to **\"Round Trip\"**.\n3. **Enter Your Stations:** \n   * **From:** Boston, MA - South Station (BOS) *or Back Bay (BBY)*\n   * **To:** New York, NY - Moynihan Train Hall at Penn Station (NYP)\n4. **Enter Your Dates:** Choose either **June 12** or **June 19** for your departure and return dates.\n5. **Select Your Trains & Seats:** Select your preferred departure times and complete the checkout using your preferred payment method. \n\n*Tip: Fridays are highly popular travel days on the Northeast Corridor. It is highly recommended to book as soon as possible, as Amtrak's dynamic pricing causes ticket costs to rise closer to the departure date.*",
